+# Private flat container seal proposal — unexecuted
+
+This is a new cache-only memory format, not a persisted Source version and not
+an interpretation of any prior admitted compact seal. It is not selected by a
+runtime. Old Work9 and both rejected method profiles remain frozen.
+
+The current container helper is fast per hit but retains three nested tuples
+and a row per original container. Its actual eleven-frame fit is only three
+entries. The proposed layout removes those per-container tuple headers while
+retaining precisely the same original container-edge proof.
+
+One seal is `(original_root, immutable_shape_bytes, immutable_refs_tuple)`.
+Every container contributes one five-byte instruction (kind and unsigned32
+length), then one contiguous reference run `[container, keys..., children...]`
+(dict) or `[container, children...]` (list). Scalar/key payload bytes are never
+copied. All original complete payload owners and Role4W remain charged.
+
+A fresh match uses one advancing tuple iterator. It checks every original
+container's current exact type and size, every original key/order and every
+current child identity. All parent edges are checked, so replaced equal child
+containers also refuse. A changed scalar's new identity refuses. Every aliased
+container occurrence is checked; cycles and foreign types are rejected at
+strict capture preflight. A size-derived total reference count prevents a
+truncated zip from becoming a successful proof. Root identity is checked too.
+Matching does not authenticate arbitrary serialized/untrusted supplied seals.
+Only an actually captured immutable, identity-pinned cache entry may be reused.
+
+Let C be container occurrences, L scalar leaf occurrences and K dictionary-key
+occurrences in the same cycle-free unfolded original graph. E=C+L−1 child
+edges. The old compact seal has S_old=5C+L shape bytes and V_old=L+K refs.
+The flat container seal has S_new=5C and V_new=C+E+K=2C+L+K−1 refs.
+With the same2048-byte header allowance:
+
+- resident delta =16C−L−8 bytes;
+- conservative construction-peak delta =32C−2L−16 bytes;
+- resident =S_new+8V_new+2048;
+- peak =2S_new+16V_new+2048+8192+1024*(selected_depth+1).
+
+The peak retains both bytearray/bytes and list/tuple transition domains even
+though construction releases the bytearray before the final ref tuple. Full
+precount precedes allocation. Capture performs a fresh complete match before
+return. The original cache's 128KiB credit,16KiB index,256B entries and all old
+residents must be subtracted before each capture; no reallocation discount,
+eviction, resealing or new quota. Cache depth/node cutoffs remain fallbacks to
+the original fresh digest and do not narrow accepted source frame grammar.
+
+This is an algebraic candidate, not a measured fit or universal allocation
+proof. Three prepared pure cases include declared-form tracemalloc and a strict
+one-byte-under-bound refusal. The separate historical eleven-frame comparison
+will show actual fits, complete prefix pass costs and unchanged original hashes.
+No cold vertical, live Source/SDK, Qt/kernel/device, whole or application claim
+can follow from those method tests alone. Actual callback/code/profile pins and
+memory-reservation selection before the first getter remain later prerequisites.
