+    V1 integer sequence <=2**53-1 needs at most16 digits. V1 bounded epoch
+    ints <=1e15 need16. An admitted positive finite binary64 has at most17
+    significant digits in Python's shortest-roundtrip JSON representation;
+    decimal point, scientific exponent and exponent sign still fit32. Quoted
+    32-character strings here overestimate that numeric serialization as well
+    as null. False is one byte longer than true. All three IDs are fixed32hex.
+    """
+    return dict(fixturePhaseVersion=1, instance='f'*32, sequence='9'*16,
+        requestId='f'*32, runId='f'*32, area='emotes', capturedEpochMs='9'*32,
+        active=False, createdEpochMs='9'*32, retiredEpochMs='9'*32)
+
