+# Private native-permit model proposal — not implemented
+
+This changes a declared host producer model, not the production Source, Native
+C++, public adapter, accepted packet grammar or any timing/capacity limit.
+The measured producer span is instrumented host-model wall time. No production
+CPU improvement or Native execution follows from correcting its guard domain.
+Frozen Work14, Work16 and Work17 implementations and evidence remain unchanged.
+
+## Actual source join
+
+| Native source | Existing host model | Proposed correspondence |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| `PicoEmoteSourceTransactionRequest::fresh` | No independent first-consumption request owner | One real monotonic/epoch pair at actual control consumption, before any builder; original five seconds, never restarted |
+| `PicoEmoteSourceArena::context/permit` | `SourceProducerModel.files.guard = original_publisher.guard` | Exact same process/birth, owning Python thread and original declared application/widget tokens; alive/stopped/failed flags; no Host Source callbacks |
+| `PicoRemoteAvatarStream::sourceTransactionPermit` | Publisher guard is `cycle.capacity.guard` | Same actual successful ARM, exact canonical Policy3 bytes/hash, enabled profile, run and original Parent baseline hash, fixed original epoch/deadline and native stream-file readiness |
+| `PicoRemoteAvatarStreamGate::fresh` | Host admission and Parent clocks are run repeatedly | One ARM-consumption clock owner, initial ARM <1.5 s, original policy end <= original epoch+120 s, armCompleted only after actual original file/readback publication |
+| `PicoEmoteSourceWidgets::available` | Indirect Host Parent/Source validation | Same original declared widget/provider object and application/thread tokens, live and not busy/failed |
+| `PicoRemoteAvatarStreamFile::ready` | Stream model currently reopens a path on write | Original writer/root descriptors created at first actual sample creation, held alias proof, fresh full bytes/full stamps/private mode/path/root proof on every readiness call |
+| Source publisher wire+receipt protocol | Fourteen `directory_guard` calls, each invokes Host capacity.guard | Keep all fourteen physical directory/file/OFD checks; substitute only the cold-selected native-domain permit callback |
+
+There is an explicit prerequisite: the current `NativeStreamModel.write` does
+not hold the original sample writer OFD. Opening the existing ARM sample later
+would adopt an older writer. The proposed model therefore owns the sample from
+its first real creation; it does not claim a late reader FD is that writer.
+
+## Exclusive files and selection
+
