+# Private Work4 memory-hash candidate — NOT application READY
+
+Only three private runtime files differ from frozen Work3: `frame_memory_digest`,
+`projected_sources.guard_bill` and `projection_semantics.functions`. No repository,
+Native, default Source2, Phone, SDK, physical originals or source DTO changed.
+The frozen17/25 packets and all previous RED evidence remain unchanged.
+
+## Exact semantic and lifetime change
+
+Every call freshly scans exact types. All-ASCII graphs use the existing strict
+`json_digest`; any Unicode uses the exact previous primitive algorithm. This
+preserves the original non-BMP-codepoint versus UTF16-surrogate-pair distinction
+which ordinary canonical JSON alone would lose. Non-JSON/subclass/metaclass,
+nonfinite, cycle and mutated-frame refusals stay enforced. No old hash/current
+verdict is cached. The new helper, strict JSON function and fallback code/defaults
+are pinned cold by the actual Source semantic owner before callbacks.
+
+A single C-JSON frame can hold text+encoded bytes up to2F, never a complete
+prefix-H buffer. Outside work leases, the actual guard bill grows16F to18F.
+During acquired work, the proposed bound uses original Work4W and old-derived16F:
+actual decoder return occurs before canonical hash callbacks, and one decoded
+candidateW plus2F hash is at most3W. No part of the separate permanent role4W is
+reused or discounted. The exact tested baseline/stored path has zero hash calls
+inside the actual decoder, four after its real return with a fresh frame still
+owned. This is an operation-boundary proof for that narrow path, NOT a universal
+proof for every future Common/capture/caller shape. SourceWork2.assert_production
+still unconditionally refuses. Full native first-builder and copy bounds remain
+incomplete, and whole560>512 SDK lower bound remains unresolved.
+
+## Qualified current cases
+
+* `memory-digest-result.json`:13 exact type/Unicode/alias/cycle/mutation cases;
+  eleven historical original frames/files unchanged.92 loaded/declared source
+  SHA+full8 signatures stable; zero late imports. Median old primitive6.724ms
