+# Pending live selection and lifetime audit
+
+This is a proposal, not an applied Source/ledger change. Work6 remains frozen.
+
+## Cold selection before any acquisition
+
+The existing single Parent, Cycle, SDK AudioRawArchive, generated-metadata
+AudioRawArchive, SourceLock and original120-second owner remain. Select the new
+codec and complete table before the metadata archive's constructor/admission.
+Persist explicit generated-metadata scope2, reference2 and reservation2 tags;
+preserve the old scope1/reference1/reservation1/default reader without rewriting
+or adopting an old bank. An original raw transaction remains format1/physical2
+and is read through its unchanged byte/hash/physical owners.
+
+Pin the exact new codec entrypoints/code/defaults and cold table bytes/identity
+under the existing Source semantic guard. The new metadata literal includes
+its complete table. Its maximum is calculated from that actual cold table and
+the existing closed schemas before the very first metadata reserve or SDK.
+The full decoded SourceFrame still has its old1MiB maximum.
+
+The current `retain_candidate` first strongly retains the already-produced
+frame and transaction, then encodes and archives metadata before any late
+business admission. Keep that order. In particular a new policy/table check
+must not be introduced in its resource-only retainer to lose an already-issued
+raw result. Capture original selected codec/table binding with the actual
+issued reservation. Existing uncertain metadata/source CAS holders persist.
+
+## Distinct byte domains
+
+The following are distinct and must not be credited twice:
+
+- Smaller canonical stored metadata: the exact new Projection2 bound only.
+- The same decoded full original frame, including both original phase graphs:
+  still charged by the existing actual logical frame bytes and16MAXF holders.
+- Full prospective SDK literalW and permanent Role4W: unchanged.
+- Existing SourceWork2 metadata transient allowance3*META_POLICY: keep its old
+  value102678 per domain until a complete callsite proof supports any change.
+- Existing unknown exception/traceback, passive replay and root/CAS allowances:
+  unchanged, not released when only a new metadata literal was sealed.
+
+## New codec overlapping representations
+
+Let B<=6656 be binary history, E<=8876 canonical Base64 characters, T the exact
+cold canonical table size, H the fixed header bound, P the maximum original
+phase canonical size, and K the guaranteed complete new wrapper size.
+
+Encoding retains the actual caller's two phase originals while constructing a
+map of canonical stimulus keys, binary history, a copied complete table/two
+headers, Base64 bytes then text, and each original phase's canonical hash
+temporaries. Hash calls are sequential but the previously constructed output
+fields and original input graphs remain. Per-row ticket/numeric/concat buffers
+are real and bounded by the fixed26-byte row format. Any exception traceback
+can retain these exact intermediates; it must retain the full current work
+claim rather than assume the successful-return overlap.
+
+Decoding retains the original stored metadata bytes/text/DTO in its actual
+caller while holding the full decoded binary, the complete After rows, an
+independent Before prefix copy, both exact headers and sequential hash buffers.
+Returning the same actual full frame never makes these output graphs absent.
+This pending document is not yet a universal byte/RSS proof. Derive the actual
+maximum overlap against the original Source callsites before applying the
+smaller reservation. Merely observing K<old metadata limit is insufficient.
+
+## Real fit proof still required
+
+The historical Work6 comparison reconstructs only original metadata literals
+from their retained ranges with SHA/full8 checks. It creates no live owner,
+issues no query and supplies no current-capacity authority. Report increases
+in small actual per-frame wrappers caused by persisting the table as well as
