+# Proposed opt-in capture-file capacity: NOT IMPLEMENTED
+
+The current13/4 Host proofs are limited and do not qualify general native-file
+capacity or canonical capture admission. Keep integrated22 and Binding frozen
+until this design is selected. No additional native control request is needed.
+
+## Typed admission before source IO
+
+1. Add optional `capacity=None` to the existing Cycle constructor. Accept only
+   exact new `PicoEmoteStreamCapacity`, already bound to this original Parent,
+   both target/role configurations, native clocks and current SourceLocks.
+   Pin the object and bound method identity in the existing config identity.
+   Default None retains existing Policy1/Budget1/native control4 behavior.
+2. Pass that exact owner during bootstrap into Policy and Originals BEFORE
+   the raw archive constructor or any ARM/source IO. Original policy and raw
+   admission clocks remain unchanged. No hot callback rebinding.
+3. Opt-in Policy2/Budget2 reads old1 and new2 explicitly. Policy2 adds a closed
+   `captureFileCapacity` POLICY object (version1): world/model/inventory maximum
+   bytes262144 each; individual storage receipt100000; one shared native pending
+   marker1024; files in the existing original private native root. These numbers
+   become actual native pre-write limits, not inferred reader limits. The same
+   actual ARM request carries Policy2; ownerPolicySha256 binds the whole tuple.
+   There is no extra control or reset of32/256/120.
+4. Originals receives the exact typed owner and pins its pure-host `bill`
+   callback before constructing AudioRawArchive. Aggregate includes the three
+   fixed native current slots+one marker from bootstrap and every issued native
+   receipt file until actual original retirement. Both host/raw/archive copies
+   and capacity journal bytes continue through the existing full root bill.
+   Existing source-only default keeps its exact original other_bill result.
+
+## Actual native guarantee, E2E Pico-only
+
+Add a small dedicated bounded capture-result publisher with original paired
+OFDs, the same Linux runtime alias requirement, exact original native root,
+closed allowed filenames and explicit pending marker/nonce. No weak fallback.
+No adoption of pre-existing result files; empty admission failure stays owned.
+
+Policy1/default Source3 saveObject code is unchanged. Only an active admitted
+Policy2 owner routes the existing world/model/inventory/storage result writes
+through this publisher. Preserve the ORIGINAL `QJsonDocument.toJson()` bytes,
+including receipt digests; do not silently switch receipt serialization.
+Write+fsync the bounded original pending intent BEFORE publishing any current
+file. Enforce the actual byte limit before first write and keep failed nonce /
+marker ownership on overflow, unknown/partial publication or alias loss.
+Advance current bytes/fullstamp only after actual same-node write/readback.
+A stale old file can never satisfy a failed nonce: world/model raw getters
+check the original pending marker before/after framing; existing native query
+request IDs remain strict. Current4 ACK/frame DTOs need no fake request ID;
+Policy2 SHA identifies the selected writer-capacity policy.
+
+Stop/drain must also account actual capture publisher writes/aliases. The
+native source remains unavailable/sticky on failed pending work; no new frame,
+control success, silent retry or file adoption. All additions remain uncompiled
+and kernel/device unqualified until separately authorized qualification.
+
+## Receipt/PNG lifetime, same aggregate
+
+The capacity owner records each ACTUAL storage command intent, before its
+existing actual native send, with the guaranteed100000-byte native file extent
+and one file count. Keep a strong pending object before construction/CAS.
+Allowances may only drop after the exact existing memory release, actual
+performed native remove and independent complete receipt absence proof plus
+own durable readback. Unknown CAS/receipt mutation retains allowance.
+
+Native GPU PNG remains its existing33554432-byte MEMORY bound; it is not
+silently reduced to16MiB or counted as disk/RSS. The validated actual capture
+metadata gives the exact encoded PNG size BEFORE the first storage chunk get.
+Reserve the actual future host PNG copy against the same aggregate at that
+boundary. If existing512/16MiB plus actual pending PNG/native files cannot fit,
+refuse before new getter and retain the issued GPU owner. Raw chunk literals,
+expanded copies and the eventual verified PNG file remain charged; release a
+pending-copy allowance only when the actual original file is accounted or its
+original ownership is authoritatively retired. No dummy files/bytes, second
+quota, namespace rotation, smaller wanted image or fresh deadline.
+
+## Targeted qualification before another component
+
+Actual default Policy1 serialization/legacy34, closed Policy2 mutation/mixed
+policy refusals, hook selected-before-first-IO/identity replacement, exact
+native file slot/receipt limits, nearcap/overflow failed-nonce marker/stale old
+file refusal, completed-lost capacity CAS/strong-OFD retention, capacity-full
+zero Native/getter, actual large PNG metadata refusal before first chunk,
+receipt allowance held through uncertain deletion and dropped only after
+independent absence. Actual native writer source checks remain uncompiled;
+host fixed-file/issuer models do not qualify Qt/kernel/GPU behavior.
